-- ==================== Aimbot (Combat tab) ====================
-- Everything here is calibrated against live measurements, not assumed:
--   * 0.002443 rad/count, both axes, exactly linear for a single large move.
--   * +X counts DECREASE world yaw; +Y counts look DOWN. Hence both negate.
--   * Angles are WORLD space. Mouse X rotates about the world vertical axis, so
--     camera-space yaw is wrong by 1/cos(pitch) (measured: 0.34863 delivered
--     where 0.36652 was expected, at 26 deg of pitch).
--   * atan2 stays defined behind the camera, so a flanking target can never
--     mirror and yank the view around - that was the close-combat "teleport".
--   * task.wait() = 21 Hz, task.wait(1/1000) = 221 Hz in Matcha.
--   * A full selection pass over ~66 targets costs 12.7 ms, so it CANNOT run
--     every tick (281% CPU). Selection is 10 Hz; tracking the locked target is
--     one 0.05 ms Position read and runs every tick.
--   * REQUIRES Windows "Enhance pointer precision" OFF. With it ON, 1-count
--     moves were only 6.3% effective (5-count 100%, 30-count 118.8%), which
--     crippled tracking. With it OFF, 1/2/4-count moves all measure 100% and
--     rad/count is identical on both axes, so MinStep 1 is correct. If aim ever
--     goes sluggish again, check that setting first.
--   * mousemoverel only takes effect while the Roblox window has focus.
--   * Camera.CFrame writes are silently discarded, which is why aim type is Mouse.
_G.AIMBOT = _G.AIMBOT or {}
